\vtwo and the systematic errors on \vtwo in \Au collisions at \sNNsixtytwo were taken from \cite{STARAuAuV0Flow}.  The dominant systematic errors were determined by comparing the reaction plane method to the four-particle cumulant method.  The four-particle cumulant method determines \vtwo by looking at correlations between four particles, which significantly reduces its sensitivity to non-flow.  \vtwo and the magnitude of the negative systematic error on \vtwo  in \Au collisions at \sNNsixtytwo as a function of \pT and centrality from \cite{STARAuAuV0Flow} are shown in \Fref{v2AuAu62}.  These were fit to a parameterization of \vtwo and the fit parameters are given in \Tref{AuAuv2FitTable}.  Statistical errors on the fits are also neglected for \Au collisions at \sNNsixtytwo since the systematic errors on \vtwo are several times larger than the statistical errors.  The positive systematic error in \Au collisions at \sNNsixtytwo is a constant, 0.003, for all centralities and \pT.

